WEBVTT

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.480
Why not ask that man?

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.240
Sho...

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:30.630
What?

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.510
Pleased to meet you, Masaki-kun.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.110
<i>Goyo Hayamichi...</i>

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.910
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:16.110
Wave 11

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:20.360
<i>A pro surfer so super famous 
that even I know about him...</i>

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.870
My older brother...

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:25.620
he said that surfing will change everything.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.620
<i>He's Sho's... older brother?</i>

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.670
Let's see...

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:35.130
Masaki-kun, and the rest of you 
as well, are Sho's friends, right?

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:36.730
That's right.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:37.630
Best friends!

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.420
Really...

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.510
Best friends, but you don't know about me?

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.870
<i>Sho's older brother... Goyo Hayamichi.</i>

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.290
<i>He's got a different last name than Sho.</i>

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.380
This is no time to be thinking!

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:15.050
<i>I'm here on the North Shore in the winter!</i>

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:18.010
<i>All I should be thinking about are 
the big waves right in front of me!</i>

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:41.950
Everyone, look at that!

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.380
Hayamichi-san.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.710
This is... my wave.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.820
That's insane!

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:06.440
He's so fast!

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.850
Hayamichi-san looks like 
he's about to take off, too!

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:19.530
Hey, that wave...

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.110
It's at least eight feet!

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:38.880
<i>It's like the first time I saw Sho surfing.</i>

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:43.420
<i>Out in the middle of the ocean, 
Hayamichi-san looks like he's shining...</i>

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.840
<i>I just can't look away!</i>

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:50.800
<i>Is he smiling?</i>

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:58.180
Hayamichi-san! That was amazing just now!

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.300
Thank you.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:07.780
Speaking of which, I saw it. 
The Forest Cup in Chiba.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.280
Really?

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.600
Sho told me, you see.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.300
He said there were a lot of 
good surfers in his generation.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:20.570
To be honest, I was expecting more.

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:21.490
Huh?

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:26.520
Fuke-kun won, rightfully so, 
and that was all.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:30.760
I thought I was going to get to see 
something more interesting.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:37.960
Well, not that I care whether 
Sho's friends are good or terrible,

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.810
but here on the North Shore, 
it puts your life at risk.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.350
Come on. Follow me.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:44.320
Huh?

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.020
You came to train, right?

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.570
I'll teach you. Myself.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.710
Your core is weak.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:16.050
Theory is good, but you should 
probably put on some muscle.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:17.270
Y-Yes, sir!

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:29.280
The surfing of a person who only thinks 
about beating others isn't very fun.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:31.240
Fun?

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.510
Don't get so hung up on winning and losing.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:36.810
Just focus on the best ride.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:37.820
Yes, sir!

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:43.080
All the waves are too big!

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.750
I can't fly with Miruru like this!

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:48.490
If you want to show her the world,

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:52.600
you need to stop focusing on air 
and work at normal riding, too.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.760
Yeah.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.880
Even the way you ride the waves is refined.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:07.530
You should show more of yourself 
in your riding and be audacious.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.530
Show more... of myself?

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:22.710
You've been doing nothing but wiping out.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.540
I-I'm sorry.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.550
It looks like you're just heading for 
every big wave that comes along,

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.940
but it isn't about just going 
for whatever wave you see.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:37.930
Masaki, you head for any wave that comes...

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.680
But just going isn't enough.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:47.690
<i>He is the one who 
taught Sho how to surf.</i>

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:54.950
<i>Hayamichi-san's surfing 
looks a lot like Sho's style.</i>

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:59.340
<i>Or rather... I guess it's Sho's style 
that looks like Hayamichi-san's.</i>

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:08.590
<i>If Hayamichi-san teaches me, 
I know I'll be able to do it, too!</i>

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:13.670
<i>I'll be able to surf like Sho!</i>

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:36.740
Masaki-kun, why did you start surfing?

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.020
Huh? Well, I...

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:41.500
It's because I saw Sho surf!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.500
I want to be like Sho!

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:46.250
That's impossible.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.110
What?

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.750
You could never be Sho.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.100
It's so good!

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:04.770
The garlic shrimp on the North 
Shore really are the best!

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.290
I wonder what's in it.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:09.490
There's butter and garlic and...

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.410
My hands are all sticky...

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:14.280
You should just eat it with the shell on.

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:16.780
Wow...

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:20.030
It's delicious either way.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.590
You could never be Sho.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.020
<i>Why would Hayamichi-san say that?</i>

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:35.550
<i>I mean, it's true that I might be 
bad compared to Sho, but...</i>

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.550
Sorry! I'm going out for a bit.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.240
You're kidding, right?

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:43.530
You're just going to leave this 
delicious food without eating it?

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:47.140
If it's too much work 
to peel it, I'll do it for you!

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.400
Corgi!

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.070
<i>Hayamichi-san.</i>

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.240
Masaki.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.060
It's a nice night, isn't it?

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:17.590
Yeah... it is.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:23.100
The truth is, I wasn't 
planning to come here.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.100
What?

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:29.970
But I heard they were getting 
big swells on the North Shore.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:34.110
And when I came, you guys were here.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:39.000
It seems like Sho really wanted 
me to meet all of you.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:46.630
Um... Can I ask you something?

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:52.630
Why did Sho start surfing?

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:55.720
Let's see...

00:10:56.130 --> 00:11:00.130
I think... he was bored.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.040
Bored?

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:05.290
Yes. Bored with everything.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.650
You, there. Are you Sho?

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:24.880
I'm Hayamichi. Do you know me?

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:27.160
I am technically your 
big brother, after all.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:28.340
Yeah.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:33.910
Let's go surfing!

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:34.680
Huh?

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:37.890
Surfing will change everything.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.990
Um... Big brother...

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:07.990
What is it?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:11.550
I think surfing is fun. I want to do more.

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:13.500
Will you teach me to surf?

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.750
Sure. No problem.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.910
Yay!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:27.010
I don't think of Sho as having died.

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:31.580
He's a surfer I trained, after all.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:32.720
And...

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:37.640
when I'm in the ocean... I can feel him.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:05.820
He did it!

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.650
That Naoya. He did it!

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:10.050
A guy like him, who's so focused on air,

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:12.850
riding a big wave like that is impressive.

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:16.710
It's all thanks to Hayamichi-san's 
targeted advice.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:20.480
Yeah. And not just Kido, the rest of us too.

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:22.030
But...

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:26.720
After coming here, Masaki-kun seems 
to have gotten thrown off his game.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:35.690
<i>Oh, what am I doing?</i>

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:38.610
<i>Forget getting better. I'm getting worse!</i>

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:45.110
<i>This is the best wave we've had 
since coming to Hawaii!</i>

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:51.240
You could never be Sho.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:55.240
<i>Then what should I be aiming for?</i>

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.540
Masaki!

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:10.000
<i>This is bad... I can't... breathe...</i>

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:12.140
<i>I told you not to push yourself too hard!</i>

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:16.750
<i>I'm sorry, Sho... I did it again...</i>

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:19.140
<i>If anything happened to you, Masaki,</i>

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:21.440
<i>a lot of people would be sad, right?</i>

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:25.600
<i>That's what I want to say to you!</i>

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:30.230
<i>Even if we're apart, we'll be 
connected through surfing.</i>

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:46.820
<i>So, show me. Show me what your 
surfing looks like, Masaki.</i>

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:49.600
<i>So that, no matter how far apart we are,</i>

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:53.930
<i>I will know that it's </i>you<i> riding 
that wave, Masaki.</i>

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:55.900
Sho...

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.090
Is he there?

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:13.770
No!

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:14.680
Masaki-kun!

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:15.600
What about over there?

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:16.950
He isn't here!

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:19.700
Masaki!

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:20.830
Masaki!

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.840
You conscious?

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:35.340
Fuke-san... Thank you...

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:38.440
Don't talk.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.670
Are you okay?

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:45.100
Are you injured?

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.110
I...

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:59.120
I... can only be me...

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:01.250
Masaki...

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:05.820
I'm sorry.

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:08.250
If I rest a little, I'll be fine.

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:14.990
If you feel even a little bit sick, 
please tell me right away.

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:17.970
I will. Thank you.

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:33.650
<i>I want to be like Sho. 
I want to surf like Sho.</i>

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:37.160
<i>But that's not enough anymore.</i>

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:41.900
<i>I... am going to surf my own way!</i>

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:34.240
<i>The show must go on!</i>

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:48.430
Masaki!

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:00.320
<i>Just now... It's like 
the wave has my back...</i>

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:03.320
<i>The ocean is telling me to go!</i>

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:45.620
Wow!

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.070
That was insane! Wow!

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.360
You really are amazing, Corgi!

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:58.950
Well done!

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:04.850
Hey.

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:07.060
Fuke-san!

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:12.690
The surfing you showed us just now 
was very close to my ideal.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:13.800
What?

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:16.350
Let's meet again, Masaki.

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.430
Y-Yes, sir!

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:23.830
It seems my little brother was right.

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:27.330
Well, I did train him, 
so I guess that should be obvious.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:28.870
Yes.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:32.330
The world will change. Through their...

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:36.400
no, through our surfing.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.110
Hawaii has been amazing!

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:07.450
Yeah, it really has.

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:09.580
I don't want to go home.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:13.600
I want to watch Miruru when it first 
broadcasts, but I don't want to go home!

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:17.130
The results of our training 
are pretty spectacular, too.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:22.500
You're sad at having to be apart 
from me again, right, Corgi?

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:25.130
That's you, not me.

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:27.310
Don't worry!

00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:30.970
You'll all come back to Hawaii soon.

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:32.520
What are you basing that on?

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:34.830
It's a sort of legend.

00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:39.800
People who see a double rainbow 
always come back to Hawaii...

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:41.150
...is what they say.

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:50.620
Yeah. I'll definitely be back!

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:52.120
Yes.

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:53.620
Yeah!

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.440
Wave 12
